      "writtenOn": "2026-08-24T21:55:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thinking about this... First, if we do that, we should rather do that for any invalid va below PAGE_OFFSET, not just for NULL? In particular, if the host is able to trick pKVM to access (e.g. write) a VA \u003d\u003d 64K, which is the start of pKVM\u0027s vmemmap, pretty bad things would happen.\n\nNow, thinking about what exactly happens if the host passes such an invalid va, e.g. NULL. __pkvm_pa(va) will return (u64)(-PAGE_OFFSET) which, with 4-level paging, is 0x10000000000000000 - 0xffff888000000000 \u003d 0x778000000000 \u003d 119.5TB which is not gonna be a RAM address with 4-level paging (systems with that much RAM use 5-level paging). So it will not pass is_memory_range() check in pkvm_host_share_hyp/pkvm_host_donate_hyp.\n\nAnd similarly with 5-level paging, __pkvm_pa(va) will be 0x10000000000000000 - 0xff11000000000000 \u003d 0xef000000000000 \u003d 59.75PB which is not gonna be a RAM address on any system.\n\nSo it seems we are safe?",
      "parentUuid": "a01a5957_48883294",
      "revId": "fd944b03fa060150e9209d000ae58ef796e3c0e7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c274826_826b5843",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/memory.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 165,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-24T22:18:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wouldn\u0027t like to require callers of kern_pkvm_va() to check the return value, as that would make it less aligned with pKVM-ARM\u0027s kern_hyp_va() and the code more complicated. If at all, I think we\u0027d rather validate __pkvm_va(phys) inside pkvm_host_share_hyp/pkvm_host_donate_hyp (since pKVM is not supposed to use a VA returned by kern_pkvm_va() until pkvm_host_share_hyp/pkvm_host_donate_hyp succeeded for it, and pKVM already takes care not to do that).\n\nAnd given the above calculations, it seems even that is not required?",
      "parentUuid": "385f7538_233ef08d",
      "revId": "fd944b03fa060150e9209d000ae58ef796e3c0e7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
